{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1245498-exalted-distilled-first-session-report","id":1245498,"title":"Exalted Distilled: First Session report","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-13T08:35:07-07:00","id":1245498,"title":"Exalted Distilled: First Session report","content":"As you may or may not know, I'm writing a slimmed down version of Exalted, where I filter out and take only what I think is necessary from Exalted for my own enjoyment. A Distillation of Exalted, or Exalted Distilled, if you may.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/138W4nP3EcmYbf4aXL6xHzgJqpsvEauRl?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">I try to keep it updated.</a><br /> <br /> I posted this on the subreddit, but I might as well do it here: the first session report. <hr /> <span style=\"color:#1C1C1C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I have to say, the first session using Exalted Distilled went really well, and I was overall very happy with it. That said, there is <i>so much left to do,</i> though: so if anyone wanted to help or collaborate, I would love it.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C1C1C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">---------------------------------------------</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C1C1C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">My players are not familiar with Exalted. I've talked to them (at great lengths) with them, and I've tried to play sessions with them. Regular Exalted was just a brick wall that they rebounded off of. Godbound was good, but the power level was way to high at the start for me. So it was my main driving force behind writing Exalted Distilled.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C1C1C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Character Creation was a bit of a chore, since this is homebrew. I kept finding things in the book I forgot to update between all of the rewrites, there were some incomplete sentences in places where my mind jumped, and of course, only the core has example charms, so the Exalted that aren't represented didn't have as much to go on.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C1C1C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">However, once we got past those hurdles, the players actually started getting really into it. I had told them &quot;Come up with an idea for a power, and I'll write it for you&quot; as a way to handle charm creation (if they are level appropriate). After a few false starts, they started coming up with more ideas, and became more invested into their characters. It was exciting to see, because my other attempts at GM'ing required a bit more...pressure to finish the character sheets.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C1C1C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">We've ended up with:</span></span></span><ul><li>A Sidereal that is so in tune with Fate she can forsee most things, and can use the Strands to entangle people in other's emotions and histories as a Martial Arts.</li> <li>A Getimian (of my best interpretation. Kinda a Nocturanal/flip-side Sidereal), who is kinda Indiana Jones/Laura Croft. Can mess with the flow of time and uses Octarine Angles of Impossibility style. (need to find the author to properly credit them.)</li> <li>A Lunar Assassin. Chameleon. So in tune with his Chameleon form that he has somewhat merged it into his human form, giving him natural access to wallwalking, changing hide, and a useful prehensile tail. Loves to stabby-stabby things. (And also attempt to steal from people when he didn't put any points into Larceny.)</li> <li>A Solar Socialite. Very good at performances, and uses the Silver-Voiced Nightengale style.</li> <li>A Solar Hammerbro. He's really good at hitting things with his hammer. Bro.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#1C1C1C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">First session might have been a bit bare bones as I had spent more time helping them get their character sheets together and plotting the frame story than planning the session, but it turned out well. My notes, mechanically:</span></span></span><ul><li>3d6 + (Attribute) +(Ability) is a bit unusual for people; it's going to take a bit getting used to--not only for them, but for me to internalize appropriate Target Numbers for tests of skill and antagonists. That said, it's not insurmountable, and is used for (almost) everything that it will become easier over time. That and dice-rolling apps get rid of that small hurdle altogether. It is a minor hurdle that I'm not super-excited to have in there, but I think the benefits outweigh the costs.</li> <li>Combat still needs to be tweaked, but this time only tweaking, not a rewrite. Attack values were too high, and defense values were too low. I think I might want to add in some level adjustment factor, like how Pathfinder has a BAB that increases with level.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":845,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","user":"Dragonmystic","date":". 08-13-2018, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}